From: M3 spike <spike@local>
Date: 2026-07-05
Subject: [PATCH 0002] ImprovedMotionDetector calibration max-frame exit

Frigate's calibration requires pct_motion < 5%, which never happens with a
looping pedestrian test clip (constant motion keeps the background model from
converging). Force calibration exit after 60 frames (12 s at 5 fps) so motion
boxes reach the object detector.

Production cameras have natural quiet intervals; this is a spike-only concern.
See docs/patches.md for rebase and upstreaming notes.
---
 frigate/motion/improved_motion.py | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/frigate/motion/improved_motion.py b/frigate/motion/improved_motion.py
--- a/frigate/motion/improved_motion.py
+++ b/frigate/motion/improved_motion.py
@@ -176,8 +176,10 @@
             motion_boxes = []
             pct_motion = 0

-        # once the motion is less than 5% and the number of contours is < 4, assume its calibrated
-        if pct_motion < 0.05 and len(motion_boxes) <= 4:
+        # once the motion is less than 5% and the number of contours is < 4,
+        # assume its calibrated; also force exit after 60 frames for constant-motion
+        # scenes (looping test clips) so the object detector receives frames.
+        if (pct_motion < 0.05 and len(motion_boxes) <= 4) or self.frame_counter >= 60:
             self.calibrating = False

         # if calibrating or the motion contours are > 80% of the image area (lightning, ir, ptz) recalibrate
